🌐 Client-Server Basics — Hinglish Notes
1. Internet & Networks ka Basic Idea

Pehle computers mostly independently kaam karte the:

Apni files store karte the
Apne programs run karte the
Dusre computers se communicate nahi karte the

Baad mein computers ko network se connect kiya gaya taaki:

Information share ho
Resources/services share ho
Distance ke across communication ho

Internet ke development mein ARPANET, CYCLADES, NPL, NSFNET jaise networks important the.

🧑‍💻 2. Client-Server Model

Client-server model mein generally:

Client request karta hai → Server service/resource provide karta hai → Server response deta hai

Example:

Browser se website open karna:

Browser = Client
Web Server = Server

Browser website ke liye request bhejta hai → Server webpage return karta hai.

⭐ Important:

Client always initiates the request.

🍕 3. Pizza Analogy

Isko yaad rakhna bahut easy hai:

Alice = User/Client
Bob = Communication method/protocol analogy
Luigi's Pizza = Server
Pizza = Requested service/resource

Flow:

Alice → Request → Bob → Luigi's → Response → Bob → Alice

Computer mein:

Client → Request → Server → Response → Client

📩 4. Request & Response
Request

Client server se kuch maangta hai.

Example:

"Mujhe website ka homepage chahiye."

Response

Server request ka result bhejta hai.

Agar resource available hai → requested content milta hai.

Agar request galat hai/resource unavailable hai → error response mil sakta hai.

⭐ Remember:

Request = Client → Server
Response = Server → Client

📜 5. Protocol

Protocol = Communication ke rules

Jaise humans ko communicate karne ke liye language/rules chahiye, waise computers ko bhi communication ke rules chahiye.

Protocol define karta hai:

Kaunse commands allowed hain
Request ka format kya hoga
Syntax kya hoga
Kis request ka kya response hoga
Faulty request par kya response dena hai
Simple definition:

Protocol = Computers ke beech communication ke rules

🚪 6. Port

Port = Specific service ko identify karne ka endpoint/door.

Ek server par multiple services run ho sakti hain.

Example analogy:

Door A → Takeaway
Door B → Dine-in
Door C → Delivery

Computer mein different services different ports par listen kar sakti hain.

🧠 Yaad rakho:

IP address = Kaunsa computer?
Port = Us computer par kaunsi service?

🌍 7. DNS

DNS = Domain Name System

DNS ka kaam:

Domain name ko IP address mein resolve karna.

Example:

example.com
⬇️ DNS
IP Address

GPS Analogy:
Website name = Place ka naam
DNS = GPS
IP address = Actual destination/address

Hum naam yaad rakhte hain; DNS us naam ko corresponding IP address se map karta hai.

🌐 8. HTTP / HTTPS

HTTP = Hypertext Transfer Protocol

Websites ke liye commonly used client-server protocol hai.

HTTPS = HTTP Secure

HTTP ko stateless protocol kaha jaata hai.

Stateless ka meaning:

Server normally har request ko independently process karta hai; previous request ki information automatically remember nahi karta.

Lekin modern websites cookies, session IDs/tokens etc. use karke login/session maintain kar sakti hain.

Example:

Login → Server session ID deta hai → Browser subsequent requests ke saath session information bhejta hai.

